From: cv610-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] hi3516cv6xx imx335: 2-lane RAW10 table for mode 0

Mode 0 (2592x1944@30) carried a 12-bit table that never writes LANEMODE
(0x3A01), so the sensor stays at its 4-lane default. On boards that wire
only two MIPI data lanes (Hi3516CV610-20S + IMX335 modules routed to PHY
lanes 0 and 2) that delivers half-width lines. Replace it with the 2-lane
RAW10 init the module's stock vendor firmware uses: LANEMODE=1, 10-bit ADC
and output, INCK 24 MHz (the sensor clock has to be set to 24 MHz to match).

--- a/libraries/sensor/hi3516cv6xx/sony_imx335/imx335_cfg.h
+++ b/libraries/sensor/hi3516cv6xx/sony_imx335/imx335_cfg.h
@@ -14,44 +14,93 @@
 #endif
 
